  + \sum_f x_{if}^2 \Sigma_f^{var} + \alpha_i^2 \Sigma_{k_i}^{AF}}

where \eqn{m_f = \sum_d S_{fd}} is the spectral mass of fluorophore f.
The spillover (multinomial), spectral-variant and AF terms are low rank,
so \eqn{\Sigma_i^{-1}} is applied via the Woodbury identity without ever
forming a D x D inverse. Abundances are clamped at zero \strong{only} when
constructing \eqn{\Sigma_i} (a variance cannot be negative); the returned
estimate is unconstrained, preserving continuity through zero.

The spillover term and shot noise (\code{diag(mu_i)/kappa}) both derive from
photon partitioning; if \code{kappa} was estimated on cell or bead data by
\code{estimate.noise.model()} (the normal case), the fitted slope has already
absorbed the spillover diagonal in full, and \code{include.spillover = TRUE}
double-counts it. Leave \code{include.spillover = FALSE} unless \code{kappa} came
from a source measured free of spillover (e.g. \verb{BDSPECTRAL QSPE}).
